WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:05.330
- I really love how you co-parent.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.380
And you have been a major
beacon of how it can be done

00:00:15.038 --> 00:00:20.038
because no parent on Earth
probably signs up to have kids

00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:25.765
and then wants to, you
know, have the plan change.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.042
How did you know to do this in this way?

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:34.382
I mean, you literally gave
a euphemism for divorce

00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:38.244
that makes us all feel
like we're saying it

00:00:38.244 --> 00:00:43.150
with a flare of dignity and hope.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.370
- Thank you.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.823
- How did you take
something broken and fix it?

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:49.350
(Gwyneth laughs)

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.782
- I mean, it's so
interesting because, like,

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:56.782
in a way my divorce and my
relationship with Chris now is,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.410
like, better than our marriage was.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.570
So, I do think that it can be done.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.820
I think, you know, there needs...

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.319
I was really lucky because I had a doctor

00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:11.492
who kinda gave us a
rubric for how to do it.

00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:13.690
And luckily he's writing a book,

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.340
and I think it's coming out
next year, thank goodness.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.410
And because it really kinda
lays out the tenets of

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.886
how you do it and it's a
little bit unsurprising, right?

00:01:23.886 --> 00:01:26.884
It's like you have to have
radical accountability.

00:01:26.884 --> 00:01:31.491
You have to know that
every relationship is 50/50

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.368
no matter what you think,

00:01:33.368 --> 00:01:35.904
how you think you were wronged or,

00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:39.174
you know, how bad you perceive
the other person's actions

00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:40.818
or whatever the case may be.

00:01:40.818 --> 00:01:42.566
If you are brave enough

00:01:42.566 --> 00:01:45.188
to take responsibility for your half

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:50.150
and really look at your own
garbage and your own trauma

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.130
and how it's presenting in the world

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.015
and in your relationship,

00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:56.710
then there's really somewhere to go

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.000
and something to learn
and something to heal.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.845
And then also you're
holding the other person

00:02:01.845 --> 00:02:05.723
in this sphere of humanity.

00:02:05.723 --> 00:02:08.074
Like, we're all part good and part bad.

00:02:08.074 --> 00:02:10.083
It's not binary.

00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.230
We're all gray area.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.121
We all are trying our best.

00:02:14.121 --> 00:02:19.121
And I really wanted my
kids to not be traumatized

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.080
if it were possible.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.079
Chris and I committed
to putting them first,

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:27.290
and that's harder than it looks

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.772
'cause some days you really don't wanna be

00:02:28.772 --> 00:02:32.289
with the person you're
getting divorced from.

00:02:32.289 --> 00:02:36.474
But if you're committed
to having family dinner

00:02:36.474 --> 00:02:37.786
then you do it.

00:02:37.786 --> 00:02:39.881
And you take a deep breath,

00:02:39.881 --> 00:02:41.252
and you look the person in the eye,

00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:43.445
and you remember your pact, and you smile,

00:02:43.445 --> 00:02:45.971
and you hug, and you make a joke,

00:02:45.971 --> 00:02:49.122
and you just re-commit
to this new relationship

00:02:49.122 --> 00:02:52.063
that you are trying to foster.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.527
- None of us wanna get
it wrong for our kids.

00:02:55.527 --> 00:02:58.684
But just because of what
happened in the marriage

00:02:58.684 --> 00:03:00.764
is not about the parenting.

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:02.947
This is about their relationship

00:03:02.947 --> 00:03:04.902
with their dad and their mom.

00:03:04.902 --> 00:03:08.214
Not about their relationship
with your marriage.

00:03:08.214 --> 00:03:09.047
- You know what?

00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:12.294
You said it, it's like
you're ending a marriage

00:03:12.294 --> 00:03:14.930
but you're still in a family.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.140
Like, that's how it will be forever.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.270
Some days it's not as good
as it looks, you know?

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.280
We also have good days and bad days,

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.970
but I think it's driving
towards the same purpose

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:30.509
of unity and love and
really what's best for them.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.947
And we have this idea that
just because we break up

00:03:32.947 --> 00:03:35.650
we can't love the things
about the person anymore

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.900
that we loved, and that's not true.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.354
- I've always seen you from
afar and wished to know you,

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:45.977
and then it was, like, finally
our timing came together and-

00:03:45.977 --> 00:03:46.810
- Thank God!

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.357
- I just marvel at you!

00:03:48.357 --> 00:03:50.336
And by the way, you're the best planner,

00:03:50.336 --> 00:03:52.958
the most cool friend,
the best sense of humor.

00:03:52.958 --> 00:03:54.798
I die over you!

00:03:54.798 --> 00:03:59.398
And I would be totally
selfish to just love up on you

00:03:59.398 --> 00:04:03.699
and not get, like, any
insider goop information,

00:04:03.699 --> 00:04:05.803
not to take a turn totally,

00:04:05.803 --> 00:04:09.845
but is there any exciting news
or things you wanna tell us

00:04:09.845 --> 00:04:12.296
so that we may better the outside

00:04:12.296 --> 00:04:15.605
after we've talked about how
we take care of our insides

00:04:15.605 --> 00:04:16.438
and our hearts?

00:04:16.438 --> 00:04:17.616
What's the 4-1-1?

00:04:17.616 --> 00:04:20.440
- Well, I have been spending,

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.493
you know, quarantine's been
a very interesting time,

00:04:23.493 --> 00:04:24.577
I think for all of us.

00:04:24.577 --> 00:04:29.388
And, you know, obviously
it's been pretty horrific

00:04:29.388 --> 00:04:30.757
in a lot of ways,

00:04:30.757 --> 00:04:33.244
but I think there has been
this wonderful silver lining

00:04:33.244 --> 00:04:35.626
of this beautiful insularity at home

00:04:35.626 --> 00:04:39.823
and with our kids and with our loved ones.

00:04:41.582 --> 00:04:43.656
But no traveling, no rushing around,

00:04:43.656 --> 00:04:45.090
so it's sort of time to sit.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.520
It's been time to sit with yourself and...

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.326
So, I sort of, like,
recommitted to a few things

00:04:50.326 --> 00:04:51.159
to feel better.

00:04:51.159 --> 00:04:55.375
Like, my meditation practice
which had been so sporadic.

00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:59.357
And making sure to move every
single day no matter what.

00:04:59.357 --> 00:05:04.357
And, like, trying to be good
with hydration and everything.

00:05:04.461 --> 00:05:06.369
But my one little beauty tip,

00:05:06.369 --> 00:05:09.487
since I was doing so many Zooms
all I could see was, like,

00:05:09.487 --> 00:05:13.465
these frown lines that I was having here.

00:05:13.465 --> 00:05:16.556
And I'm really lucky

00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:19.332
'cause one of my closest
friends is a plastic surgeon.

00:05:19.332 --> 00:05:20.954
His name is Julius and
he lives in Chicago,

00:05:20.954 --> 00:05:22.662
and I'm always asking him, like,

00:05:22.662 --> 00:05:25.525
what's the thing coming down the road?

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:29.540
And he gave me a teeny drop
of this thing called Xeomin

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:34.540
which is a purified ant-wrinkle injection.

00:05:35.761 --> 00:05:39.060
And I just feel like...

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.010
It was purified.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.760
It's like a uniquely purified formula.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.323
So, I'm like, "Okay, this
is in the wellness world."

00:05:45.323 --> 00:05:48.923
And it was a Zoom face curer for me.

00:05:48.923 --> 00:05:52.340
(upbeat pop music plays)

